#!/bin/bash
# Crypto V7 COIN PAGE TRUTH loop — self-paced, read roadmap and execute first unchecked task
# Run: claude "/loop $(tail -1 CRYPTO_LOOP_V7.sh)"
# Or paste the last line into claude with /loop

Read docs/CRYPTO_V7_COINPAGE_ROADMAP.md and follow its doctrine and hard rules exactly. Do only the first unchecked [ ] task. Doctrine recap: TRUTH — honest empty-state beats plausible numbers, NEVER render another asset's data, every fetch keyed by CG id + venue from cryptoStore base rows (never bare symbol). DESIGN FREEZE — keep each tab's existing layout/tokens/markup, swap the data source only; empty states reuse existing empty-state styling. ONE SOURCE RULE: coin-page prices go through livePrice(row, spotRow); chart last-candle tick is the only exception and it is gate-checked. NO new serverless files (?view= branches in api/crypto/markets.ts; news.ts and klines.ts may be edited) — Hobby 12-function cap. Keyless APIs only and curl-verify each new endpoint shape from prod (fra1) before coding (CG /coins/{id} slim params, /tickers?depth=true, /market_chart daily; yields.llama.fi/pools). CG free tier 429s: per-coin blobs via cachedBlob (profile 24h, tickers 15m, mcapchart 1h), lazy fetch on tab open only, never prefetch 200 profiles. OKX candles are newest-first — reverse. No new npm deps; vercel.json keeps regions fra1. Verify per task: market-ui typecheck 0 + vercel --prod (from repo root — apps/market-ui path breaks the project link) + prod curl with real numbers + audit green (spot 200/200, MISMATCH 0) + GRAM spot-check (its About/Holders/Markets/chart must never show BTC or another coin's data). Flip the task to [x], append one Progress-log line with real numbers, commit on roadmap/world-class (git commit -F file if the message has quotes — rtk mangles them). PERSISTENCE: never end the loop because of a usage/rate limit, 429, or overloaded error — on any such error stop consuming tokens, ScheduleWakeup at 3600s with this exact /loop prompt, and on wake re-read the ledger and resume the same task from its last verified step (ledger + Progress log are recovery state; log partial progress BEFORE long/risky operations); chain hourly wakeups as needed. Only stop for: no [ ] remaining, or a task blocked on something only the user can provide — then say exactly what's needed and still ScheduleWakeup (3600s) so the loop resumes if supplied.
